<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>No boards yet</title>
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 40px 20px;
        background: {{ palette.panel_bg }};
        color: {{ palette.text }};
        font-family: {{ palette.font_family | safe }};
      }
      main { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.5; }
      h1 { color: {{ palette.accent }}; font-size: 1.8rem; }
      pre {
        padding: 14px 18px;
        border: 1px solid {{ palette.border }};
        border-radius: 8px;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      a { color: {{ palette.accent }}; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>No boards yet</h1>
      <p>
        A board is one YAML file: some queries, and the charts that draw them.
        This page lists every board in the project, and it stays here until
        there is one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Add a <code>.yml</code> file under <code>charts/</code>, for example
        <code>charts/sales.yml</code>, and reload:
      </p>
      <pre>title: Sales
queries:
  by_month:
    type: values
    columns: [month, revenue]
    values:
      - [Jan, 120]
      - [Feb, 150]
      - [Mar, 190]
charts:
  revenue:
    type: bar
    query: by_month
    x: month
    y: revenue</pre>
      <p>
        A query can also be <code>sql:</code> against a warehouse instead of <code>type: values</code>;
        see the <a href="{{ docs_url }}">docs</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
